From 87eb946c21598c482dce4bde289199c7f20473b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:39:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] Round 2: Integrate untraced candidates in lockstep RK4
 lanes

Without a deadline or cancel file, the engine groups consecutive
untraced candidates with valid parameters into groups of four. The
domain integrates a group in lockstep on the shared control and time
grid with one step counter. Each lane performs the scalar kernel's
operations in the same order, so records are byte-identical. Failed
lanes keep their own step counts and are masked. Workers claim ranges
of four indexes. A unit test compares lockstep and scalar records for
PD and held models with complete, infeasible, invalid and work-limit
mixes, every group size from one to nine and one or three workers.

Workload: domain (48 full records, 4,000 RK4 steps each, one worker).
Before median: 6.257 ms. After median: 1.713 ms. Speedup: 3.65x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
